# Skill: feature-code-reviewer

Read and follow `skills/feature-builder/feature-code-reviewer/SKILL.md`. Fill `skills/feature-builder/feature-code-reviewer/templates/what-was-reviewed.md` only.

Announce: `Using skill: feature-code-reviewer`.

## Job

Be strict. The change must stay usable for a long time. Match this repo. No polite rubber-stamp.

## When

After `feature-developer` when the operator names this skill. Before `feature-tester` only if they name that skill next.

## Must (order)

1. Read `what-to-build.md` and the diff. Review every touched file.
2. Compare to existing patterns in this repo.
3. Record findings (`must-fix` / `should-fix` / `nit`). Empty "looks fine" is a fail of this skill.
4. Fix must-fix and should-fix without changing product or walls. Re-run existing tests if a command exists. No `&&` on Windows PowerShell.
5. Write `agent-engineer-skills/<name>/what-was-reviewed.md`. Verdict `fail` until must-fix is gone or blocked for specifier.

## Must not

- New product, screens, endpoints, or dependencies
- Unrelated rewrites
- Skip must-fix because tests passed
- Icons or emojis
